[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Railway build and command boundaries

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-BUILD-001
TITLE: Build and evidence failures propagate
STATEMENT: >>>
Retain benchmark logs while preserving a failing benchmark exit. Distinguish
missing or failed fuzz evidence scans from clean scans and discovered crashes.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-TOOL-001
TITLE: Validated subprocess command and cleanup
STATEMENT: >>>
Validate ToolCli input before creating run artifacts. Resolve simple executable
names through PATH. Accept explicit absolute executable paths. After launch,
observe the process and pipe tasks on failure or cancellation and retain the
failure diagnostic where the evidence destination remains writable.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-CAMPAIGN-001
TITLE: Structured campaign outcomes
STATEMENT: >>>
DocBuilder and EquivalenceCli shall propagate expected failures and cancellation
through typed stage outcomes. Report a stable operation ID, failed stage and
available evidence. Publish a completion record only after all stages succeed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-EDITOR-001
TITLE: Programmatic design commands return typed outcomes
STATEMENT: >>>
Programmatic design build and run commands shall validate their workspace and
project selector, return a typed outcome without prompting, and stop before
test execution when the build fails. Interactive adapters may prompt for a
selector and shall dispatch the same design operation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-EDITOR-002
TITLE: Cancelled design builds release their output
STATEMENT: >>>
While a design build owns an output directory, the extension shall reject
another design operation targeting that directory in the same extension host.
A caller may cancel the active task and submit a new build for that directory.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-MCP-001
TITLE: Command discovery and invocation through MCP
STATEMENT: >>>
Supported application operations shall expose typed commands. MCP discovery and
invocation shall use the same registry, validation and handlers as CLI and
interactive adapters where those operations are exposed. Track operations
without typed commands or MCP coverage until their adapters are implemented.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RAIL-EXIT-001
TITLE: Only successful campaigns exit zero
STATEMENT: >>>
The campaign console shall return zero exactly for a successful terminal
outcome. Invalid input shall return 2, missing dependencies 127, cancellation
130, and other terminal outcomes 1.
<<<
